 "_about": "Real 360° photographs (equirectangular panoramas) from Wikimedia Commons, one per expedition, for the 'Look around for real' viewpoint. tools/fetch-expedition-panoramas.mjs searches Commons with each entry's terms, keeps only 2:1 equirectangular JPEGs at least 3000 px wide that are filed as panoramas and whose title or categories match a `must` pattern, saves them into games/photo-expedition/panoramas/ and writes panoramas/manifest.js with the credit. Entries are tried in order; a site with no suitable panorama simply has no viewpoint. Most 360° photographs on Commons come from Mapillary imports and phone photo-spheres, so the search terms pair a place with the cameras that shoot them (LG-R105, Ricoh Theta, Insta360, Gear 360, GoPro Max) or the words photosphere / 360° panorama.",
